  "known_limitations": [
    "M4 classifies stale executions as interrupted but does not implement M5 checkpointed continuation, durable budget recovery or exact resume.",
    "The bundled supervisor is single-process and serial; it is not a distributed queue or multi-worker scheduler.",
    "A timed-out Python thread cannot be forcibly stopped. Lease, revision and callback fencing prevent publication, but shared provider resources still need stronger process or executor isolation.",
    "SSE replay is durable but currently polls PostgreSQL; higher fan-out may require LISTEN/NOTIFY or a separate event delivery layer while retaining the database log.",
    "Static bearer-token mapping is suitable for controlled deployment and tests, not a replacement for production OIDC, TLS termination, rate limiting, secret rotation, audit and retention controls.",
    "Provider-free acceptance proves service wiring and safety invariants, not live-model quality, legal correctness, complete current-law coverage or production latency.",
    "The package declares Python >=3.10, while the authoritative release CI environment is Python 3.12.13; a wider interpreter matrix remains desirable.",
    "GitHub Actions emitted a non-blocking Node 20 deprecation warning for actions/upload-artifact while forcing Node 24; the pinned action should be upgraded later.",
    "The repository-wide Ruff format baseline contains legacy differences, and full Ruff lint still has a pre-existing F841 in legal_rag/indexing.py; M4 used targeted lint and did not mass-format unrelated files.",
    "If shutdown leaves a quarantined execution thread alive, the service conservatively retains its engine and pool until that thread drains; repeated in-process hot reload can therefore retain old pools temporarily.",
    "The default HTTP path rebuilds the frozen corpus and BM25 retriever for each run; full-corpus cache behavior, memory consumption and P95/P99 latency have not received release-grade benchmarking.",
    "Readiness performs bounded serving-boundary checks rather than a full row-by-row corpus audit, and the default HTTP route does not yet expose exact dense, catalog or experimental HNSW retrieval.",
    "Alembic 0005 downgrade deletes all M4 session, run, message, result, idempotency and event history and therefore requires an explicitly approved backup and rollback procedure."
  ],
